<Section id="lines" title="4. Drawing Line Charts">

A `<line>` joins two points. It needs a start (`x1`, `y1`) and an end (`x2`, `y2`), plus a `stroke`:

```svelte
/// file: A line
<svg class="chart" width="500" height="350">
	<line x1="50" y1="280" x2="160" y2="50" stroke="tomato" stroke-width="2" />
</svg>
```

- `x1`, `y1` set where the line **starts**; `x2`, `y2` where it **ends**.
- `stroke` is the line's colour and `stroke-width` its thickness. A line has no `fill` because it's not a filled in shape.

To turn the scatter plot into a line chart, draw a `<line>` between each dot and the next, reusing the very positions you plotted the circles at. Draw the lines first so the dots sit on top:

<Exercise file="3-connect-the-dots.svelte">
	<ConnectTheDots />
</Exercise>

{#snippet sidebar()}

One line between two dots:

```svelte
/// file: Line
<line x1="50" y1="280" x2="160" y2="50" stroke="tomato" stroke-width="2" />
```

